Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 5a67796fc7b21276b368a355bd58c9fddc3bd780&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="505804" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:51:35 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Patch: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70882" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70882&lt;/a&gt;. A run with the fix and nonblk_zcack=0 will be added here.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="505807" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:13:59 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Tested 70882 between two Rocky 10 VMs (6.12 kernel) over a fast virtio-net switch, LNet selftest 1 MB writes and reads with 8 and 32 in flight, 30 second windows, two repeats (4 minutes of bulk traffic) with nonblk_zcack=0 on both nodes: no oops, no errors. Without the fix the same setup oopses within 2 seconds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With the fix, nonblk_zcack=0 is no slower than the default and may be faster for reads, where the ZC-ACK can ride on the LNet ACK (two runs each, GB/s):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;```&lt;br/&gt;
                 nonblk_zcack=0 + fix   nonblk_zcack=1 + fix   stock, nonblk_zcack=1&lt;br/&gt;
write, 8 in flight   2.38 / 2.69            1.96 / 2.47            2.38 / 2.40&lt;br/&gt;
read, 8 in flight    2.23 / 2.31            1.89 / 1.85            1.72 / 2.06&lt;br/&gt;
```&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
